From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MinsOS <minsos@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Treat an unknown UICC apps state as enabled (One UI 9, y2q)

GsmCdmaPhone.isUiccApplicationsEnabled() returned false while
mUiccApplicationsEnabled is null, that is, while no successful answer to
GET_UICC_APPLICATIONS_ENABLEMENT has arrived. The query is sent once, at radio
available. When the S20+ boots without a SIM the A13 RIL answers SIM_ABSENT,
nothing asks again when a SIM is inserted, and the RIL sends no
UNSOL_UICC_APPLICATIONS_ENABLEMENT_CHANGED. SubscriptionManagerService
.isSubscriptionEnabled() then stays false for the active SIM and PhoneSwitcher
on a KOR build never picks a data phone, so mobile data never connects.
Unknown now reads as enabled, as the donor's own
reapplyUiccAppsEnablementIfNeeded() already treats it ("do nothing"), and the
stock A13 framework has no such gate. An explicit false from the RIL still
disables, and the user's per-SIM switch is still checked through
SubscriptionInfoInternal.areUiccApplicationsEnabled().
---
diff --git a/smali/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone.smali b/smali/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone.smali
--- a/smali/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone.smali
+++ b/smali/com/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone.smali
@@ -15837,15 +15837,15 @@
 .method public blacklist isUiccApplicationsEnabled()Z
     .locals 0
 
     iget-object p0, p0, Lcom/android/internal/telephony/GsmCdmaPhone;->mUiccApplicationsEnabled:Ljava/lang/Boolean;
 
     if-nez p0, :cond_0
 
-    const/4 p0, 0x0
+    const/4 p0, 0x1
 
     return p0
 
     :cond_0
     invoke-virtual {p0}, Ljava/lang/Boolean;->booleanValue()Z
 
     move-result p0
